            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did paṇṭa mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: గోడ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గోడ (gōḍa) — \"a wall\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గోడ (gōḍa) is a wall: the built side of a room. A village house puts up four of them in mud or in brick, and everything after that — the తలుపు, the కుర్చీ pushed back against one of them — is placed by where they stand."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is inherited, and it does the same figurative work English asks of a wall. Somebody who will not listen is a గోడ (gōḍa), and a family with nothing hidden has no గోడ (gōḍa) inside it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Whitewashing the గోడ (gōḍa) before a festival is its own small season in a Telugu house. A guest who arrives to a fresh one has been told they were expected, and the right thing to say at that moment is నమస్కారం."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One. What a house is measured by before anything is put inside it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "gōḍa",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *gōḍa*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "gōḍa, then namaskāram, as though greeting somebody at a freshly painted one",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *gōḍa*, then *namaskāram*, as though greeting somebody at a freshly painted one]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does గోడ (gōḍa) mean? (\"a wall\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
