        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: కప్పు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కప్పు (kappu) — \"a roof\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కప్పు (kappu) is the roof — the thing that covers. It comes from the same stem as the everyday word for covering something over, so a lid on a గిన్నె and the roof over a room are one idea in Telugu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Village roofs were గడ్డి over beams for centuries and are tile or concrete now. The material changed and the word did not, which is usually a sign of a very old one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "To be under somebody's కప్పు (kappu) is to be their guest, and it binds the person underneath as much as the person above. నమస్కారం comes first, and everything else follows it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: గోడ (gōḍa) and కప్పు (kappu). Sides, and a lid."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kappu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kappu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "gōḍa, then kappu, and say which one holds up the other",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *gōḍa*, then *kappu*, and say which one holds up the other]"
            }
          ]
        },
