          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మెట్టు (meṭṭu) — \"a step\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మెట్టు (meṭṭu) is a step — one of a flight, cut in stone or built up in mud."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Telugu counts them and remembers them. The steps down to a చెరువు are named in some villages, and a house with a మెట్టు (meṭṭu) at its గడప (gaḍapa) is a house standing a little above the street."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word carries rank as well. A person who has risen has climbed a మెట్టు (meṭṭu), which is how a stair turns into a career with nobody explaining it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four. Something to climb before you cross."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
