        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: కిటికీ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కిటికీ (kiṭikī) — \"a window\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కిటికీ (kiṭikī) is a window. It is a borrowing, ultimately from Portuguese, and it arrived carrying the shape of window it names: a framed opening in a గోడ (gōḍa), rather than the small unglazed gap older houses left for గాలి."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Telugu kept the borrowed word and the older habit side by side. A కిటికీ (kiṭikī) is opened at ఉదయం, shut against the sun in the middle of the day, and opened again by సాయంత్రం."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A house with a గోడ (gōḍa), a కప్పు (kappu), a గడప (gaḍapa), a మెట్టు (meṭṭu) and a కిటికీ (kiṭikī) is a whole house. Whoever is standing at any one of them is somebody you can greet."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: గోడ (gōḍa), కప్పు (kappu), గడప (gaḍapa), మెట్టు (meṭṭu), కిటికీ (kiṭikī). A house you could walk up to and greet."
            }
          ]
        },
